In general, you don't want your v.o. to sound like it was written. Not an essay, not an idea of what a script should sound like, and definitely not like AI. SO how do you achieve that?

The easiest answer is the same as my hot take for every aspect of marketing; follow the data. 

What is the easiest way to identify videos that work? Your own data, your influencer data, and third-party marketplaces like TikTok Shop or LTK. The girls who know how to sell, also know how to speak. 

The most successful influencer videos I've ever contracted have provided high level guidelines, ensuring the creator understands the product and the brand, but then leaves them to speak to their audience in a way that is totally natural for their channel. That's exactly what you want to replicate for organic and paid content. The best part is, you have a wealth of information at your fingertips. Creative strategists who want to prove their expertise for B2B marketing highlight their top wins, AI agents can surface to you ads that have been live the longest for your competitors. Dissect those patterns and get tot esting. 

And I hear you already...but how do I know what part of the script works? What if everything sucks, how do I dissect my scripts? Well, once again, I say...follow the data!

See the scrollstopping series to understand the components of a strong video, and check crative-workflows for some insights of what different indicators signal about what is and is not working. From there, start to break things down. Did you get people to stay past the first 5 seconds, but they didn't convert? And did that happen across creative and visual styles while you repurposed the same scripting formula or verbiage? Well, now you know to start looking at the body and the action to breakdown what may and may not work. Don't just tweak a word or two. Read it to yourself, rewatch the content as the consumer. And think critically about what failed. The comments can be a great insight finding tool. Have AI read through them and distill takeaways. How many people are complaining about the way the creator spoke or a forced affect? That is likely a problem with the script. Especially if you've hired a strong UGC personality or a popular influencer who earns repeated brand deals. You might just be the problem. Now figure out how to fix it.
